  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/e1d5eb2f392332f69fa1507899b30b838a42ebd1c40dacddeca4edcf0f7aa8c2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=-b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/0e8e24968141284550fac7d4e5c63333789f30ade8f7d5dd8b87fae4e012673a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =a+(-b) \\\\  & =a-b\\end{aligned}\n$$",
